                    {
                        "form_id": "4e829e55-4a86-4af2-b609-eaff37d79d1f",
                        "entry_id": "588df870-8610-30f1-b057-80d469a3c1f5",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "позитиви́стах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "054713ae-62ac-399c-a759-9bda86d22a67",
                        "entry_id": "588df870-8610-30f1-b057-80d469a3c1f5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "человек, исповедующий позитивизм"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "50f4b1ba-cebf-4320-886a-db229ec9c3bc",
                                "sense_id": "054713ae-62ac-399c-a759-9bda86d22a67",
                                "text": "Философ, какого бы он ни был толка — идеалист, спиритуалист, пессимист, позитивист, — на вопрос: зачем он живет так, как он живет, то есть несогласно с своим философским учением?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "26c02050-7723-4018-b80e-31c4fe05cd60",
                        "source_entry_id": "588df870-8610-30f1-b057-80d469a3c1f5",
                        "source_sense_id": "054713ae-62ac-399c-a759-9bda86d22a67",
                        "target_lang_word": "positivist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "positivist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9446d007-48e2-38aa-8367-491bef5cbd6c",
                                        "entry_id": "0572f650-9ac0-3376-89ae-b0d2035057f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Related to positivism, positivistic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2620b84e-5307-449e-ae02-f6b47e723593",
                                                "sense_id": "9446d007-48e2-38aa-8367-491bef5cbd6c",
                                                "text": "The positivist tradition contains some rigorous, well-argued and stimulating methodological discussions; such material should be required reading for qualitative researchers wishing to enhance the quality of their practice."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6075e4c4-db9e-432b-9d3d-ef73c9245446",
                                                "sense_id": "9446d007-48e2-38aa-8367-491bef5cbd6c",
                                                "text": "Making use of the conceptual vocabulary of science to exclude a possibility that in a present state of knowledge—or a former one—that vocabulary would seem to exclude, has been the mission of positivist thinking since Auguste Comte declared scientific knowledge effectively complete."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97aedc81-8765-41a3-bd7a-e2986e91fe8c",
                                                "sense_id": "9446d007-48e2-38aa-8367-491bef5cbd6c",
                                                "text": "While a positivist view of history—the 19th-century notion that history was akin to a science, and that the accumulation of historical facts would eventually lead to an objective understanding of events—fell out of favor long ago, this idea seems to remain the operative assumption behind traditional history curricula that emphasize content, chronology, and comprehensiveness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "positivist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e534968d-09f0-3750-9e77-21b9ee355f96",
                                        "entry_id": "35817992-085d-3cd5-96c2-4e44ae26b361",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A believer in positivism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e2a4ebc-10a8-42a0-84d3-7f207afd0926",
                                                "sense_id": "e534968d-09f0-3750-9e77-21b9ee355f96",
                                                "text": "The English mind is prone to positivism and kindred forms of materialistic philosophy, and we must expect the derivative theory to be taken up in that interest. We have no predilection for that school, but the contrary. If we had, we might have looked complacently upon a line of criticism which would indirectly, but effectively, play into the hands of positivists and materialistic atheists generally."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "feda6d28-391d-4cf7-babb-28f803c6430c",
                                                "sense_id": "e534968d-09f0-3750-9e77-21b9ee355f96",
                                                "text": "By discouraging what they conceive to be the weakness of their master, the English Positivists have broken the strength of their religion. A man who has faith must be prepared not only to be a martyr, but to be a fool."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b2afabd-2f16-468d-b29a-bb6a71354a2d",
                                                "sense_id": "e534968d-09f0-3750-9e77-21b9ee355f96",
                                                "text": "A modern intellectual comes in and sees a poker. He is a positivist; he will not begin with any dogmas about the nature of man, or any day-dreams about the mystery of fire. He will begin with what he can see, the poker; and the first thing he sees about the poker is that it is crooked."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60836fb8-d9a1-4038-8019-3374202ce61a",
                                                "sense_id": "e534968d-09f0-3750-9e77-21b9ee355f96",
                                                "text": "Shall we erect the mystery into an Unknowable, like Spencer, and call ourselves Agnostics with a capital letter, like Huxley? Shall we follow Frederic Harrison, making an inadequate divinity out of our impotence? I have read the books of the \"Positivists\", and attended their imitation church in London, but I did not get any satisfaction from them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1725fa11-dbb7-4ec8-bcdf-79bcd42cb984",
                                                "sense_id": "e534968d-09f0-3750-9e77-21b9ee355f96",
                                                "text": "However vigorously he may assert that he is a pure positivist, who has long left behind him supernatural tendencies and weaknesses, and now accepts only what is immediately certain, he will never be free of the secret uncertainty whether positivism really has the last word."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a22bf4c-766b-4312-bc6a-7e9d3e64d29c",
                                                "sense_id": "e534968d-09f0-3750-9e77-21b9ee355f96",
                                                "text": "Freedom of expression tends to be associated primarily with nineteenth-century English philosopher John Stuart Mill, whose treatise On Liberty is most frequently reached for by freedom of expression positivists, although it did not mention any “free marketplace” of ideas."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b6dedc7c-f653-4e45-b12c-4238c30411d5",
                        "source_entry_id": "588df870-8610-30f1-b057-80d469a3c1f5",
                        "source_sense_id": "054713ae-62ac-399c-a759-9bda86d22a67",
                        "target_lang_word": "positivista",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "869f5064-54eb-45cf-84df-f7a0e7c71449",
                        "source_entry_id": "588df870-8610-30f1-b057-80d469a3c1f5",
                        "source_sense_id": "054713ae-62ac-399c-a759-9bda86d22a67",
                        "target_lang_word": "positivista",
                        "target_lang_code": "it",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "positivista",
                                "target_lang_code": "it",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e1c0a9f9-e0bb-3267-9011-888d70c60d34",
                                        "entry_id": "df7a4e0f-298a-386b-b57e-8c1d2289a4e0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "che concerne il positivismo"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79499982-8944-399f-a3be-ed9455aa8b3a",
                                        "entry_id": "df7a4e0f-298a-386b-b57e-8c1d2289a4e0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "che, anche nelle relazioni sociali, è scevra da elementi contraddittori o negativi, quindi scientificamente diretta a cose e/o fatti duraturi e veri, sia interiori, spirituali, intellettivi sia materiali"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f425c8f-fd2d-45f3-b48d-d91bcf52a8fd",
                                                "sense_id": "79499982-8944-399f-a3be-ed9455aa8b3a",
                                                "text": "pensiero positivista"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "positivista",
                                "target_lang_code": "it",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "64701a0e-7250-34c0-9ca3-4f2aadc597ff",
                                        "entry_id": "23f4d7d5-1fa6-3859-b631-832b61d0da68",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "seguace del positivismo"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9e226dad-26f4-45d5-8fed-d9dc8e79eeb2",
                        "source_entry_id": "588df870-8610-30f1-b057-80d469a3c1f5",
                        "source_sense_id": "054713ae-62ac-399c-a759-9bda86d22a67",
                        "target_lang_word": "positiviste",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "positiviste",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57325e4e-4d5b-3d54-8df8-ab1e51255235",
                                        "entry_id": "7b761d5d-ba6b-38a7-a5e8-f952a8c3d9ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relatif à la doctrine d’Auguste Comte."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6b9b2e45-4263-4949-a5fa-5bb21a0444ab",
                                                "sense_id": "57325e4e-4d5b-3d54-8df8-ab1e51255235",
                                                "text": "Le dogme, la morale, la politique positiviste."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d52de38-9f0f-46f6-b2e3-62ee319d969c",
                                                "sense_id": "57325e4e-4d5b-3d54-8df8-ab1e51255235",
                                                "text": "Plus tard, venu à Paris comme petit professeur, passionné par l’étude, il s’était donné, de toute son intelligence, à Auguste Comte ; et c’était ainsi qu’on aurait retrouvé chez lui, sous le positiviste fervent, l’ancien proudhonien, sa révolte personnelle de pauvre, en haine de la misère."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6dfe6d94-bd65-425a-a183-55b837de5f3b",
                                                "sense_id": "57325e4e-4d5b-3d54-8df8-ab1e51255235",
                                                "text": "Ensuite, il faut se débarrasser de cette culture positiviste qui considère la technique comme « neutre » et moralement soumise au seul usage qui en sera fait par l’utilisateur."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "positiviste",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8a3e3c0a-a97a-3dbc-9673-3f2809d0dc2c",
                                        "entry_id": "6251a1b2-c753-3f9b-88b8-201dc65164a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Adepte du positivisme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba056166-e545-45b8-97bd-a115b3bc690b",
                                                "sense_id": "8a3e3c0a-a97a-3dbc-9673-3f2809d0dc2c",
                                                "text": "En sciences humaines, un positiviste sera donc celui qui valorise ou adopte le modèle de la science positive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d87db2c9-f063-4ed6-86e4-dac0dbdd8e27",
                                                "sense_id": "8a3e3c0a-a97a-3dbc-9673-3f2809d0dc2c",
                                                "text": "Les positivistes, qui représentent, à un degré éminent, la médiocrité, l’orgueil et le pédantisme, avaient décrété que la philosophie devait disparaître devant leur science ; mais la philosophie n’est point morte et elle s’est réveillée avec éclat."
                                            },
                                            {
